  "description": "Spacious, sought after location walking distance to all city centre amenities.  Rowan Fitzgerald Auctioneers are delighted to present 14 The Orchards to the Limerick sales market.  The property is situated in a select and quiet cul de sac whilst enjoying the benefits of a large private corner site. The home enjoys the conveniency of being within short walking distance of Mary Immaculate College, Local Shops and The City Centre. The location is also just off the dock road which leads to major roads such as the N69 and N18 and also easy access to the M7.\nThis extra spacious 5 bedroom semi-detached property is located in a private cul-de-sac avenue not overlooked to the rear and extra privacy is offered by the trees to the front.  This is a large, bright and spacious home and needs to be seen to be fully appreciated. \nAccommodation comprises of an entrance hall off which there is a living room which benefits from double doors leading to the open plan kitchen/dining room.  Off the Kitchen is a Utility room with guest WC.  To the front of the house there is a ground floor double sized bedroom with en-suite, this completes the ground floor accommodation.\nUpstairs, there are 4 bedrooms, 3 of which are double sized and 1 is a single.  The master bedroom is en-suite and the main bathroom completes the accommodation. \nViewing comes highly recommended, for more information or to arrange a viewing, please call Rachael on 061-279423 or email reply to this advert. \nDisclaimer: These particulars and terms are provided by Rowan Fitzgerald Auctioneers with the understanding that all negotiations regarding the mentioned property must be conducted exclusively through them. While every effort has been made to ensure the accuracy of the information provided, Rowan Fitzgerald Auctioneers makes no warranties, express or implied, regarding the particulars or any representations made about the property. The details in this brochure do not form any part of a contract. 